  python  graphql.print_schema, graphql.print_type, graphql.print_directive, graphql.print_introspection_schema, strawberry.printer
  note    graphql-js's `printSchema`, byte for byte on the probed schemas

capability schema/code-first  a schema built from the program's own types and functions
  heroes  refused: a schema is written in GraphQL's own schema language and read by `parse_schema`; deriving it from the program's types needs the reflection, macros or decorators the language refuses, and building it from values would be a second way to write the same text
  go      graphql-go NewSchema, SchemaConfig, Schema, NewObject, ObjectConfig, Object, NewInterface, InterfaceConfig, Interface, NewUnion, UnionConfig, Union, NewEnum, EnumConfig, Enum, EnumValueConfig, EnumValueConfigMap, EnumValueDefinition, NewInputObject, InputObjectConfig, InputObject, InputObjectField, InputObjectFieldConfig, InputObjectConfigFieldMap, NewScalar, ScalarConfig, Scalar, NewList, List, NewNonNull, NonNull, NewDirective, DirectiveConfig, Directive, Fields, Field, FieldConfigArgument, ArgumentConfig, Argument, FieldArgument, FieldDefinition, FieldDefinitionMap, BindFields, BindArg, FieldsThunk, InterfacesThunk, UnionTypesThunk, InputObjectConfigFieldMapThunk, SerializeFn, ParseValueFn, ParseLiteralFn, Type, Input, Output, Leaf, Composite, Abstract, Nullable, Named, GetNamed, GetNullable, TypeMap
  rust    async-graphql attributes Object, ComplexObject, Subscription, Scalar, Directive, TypeDirective, derives SimpleObject, InputObject, Enum, Interface, Union, OneofObject, MergedObject, MergedSubscription, NewType, Description, traits ObjectType, InputType, OutputType, InterfaceType, UnionType, InputObjectType, OneofObjectType, SubscriptionType, TypeName, ContainerType, EnumType, ScalarType, macros scalar, dynamic::Schema, SchemaBuilder, Object, Field, FieldFuture, FieldValue, InputObject, InputValue, Interface, InterfaceField, Union, Enum, EnumItem, Scalar, Directive, Subscription, SubscriptionField, SubscriptionFieldFuture, TypeRef, Type, ResolverContext, ValueAccessor, ObjectAccessor, ListAccessor, DynamicRequest, DynamicRequestExt, SchemaError, EmptyMutation, EmptySubscription; juniper attributes graphql_object, graphql_interface, graphql_union, graphql_scalar, graphql_subscription, derives GraphQLObject, GraphQLInputObject, GraphQLEnum, GraphQLInterface, GraphQLUnion, GraphQLScalar, ScalarValue, traits GraphQLType, GraphQLValue, GraphQLTypeAsync, GraphQLValueAsync, GraphQLObject, GraphQLInterface, GraphQLUnion, GraphQLSubscriptionType, GraphQLSubscriptionValue, FromInputValue, ToInputValue, IntoInputValue, IntoValue, IsInputType, IsOutputType, ParseScalarValue, FromScalarValue, ToScalarValue, ScalarValue, TryToPrimitive, Registry, EmptyMutation, EmptySubscription, the `meta` types
  python  graphql.GraphQLSchema, GraphQLObjectType, GraphQLInterfaceType, GraphQLUnionType, GraphQLEnumType, GraphQLEnumValue, GraphQLInputObjectType, GraphQLInputField, GraphQLScalarType, GraphQLList, GraphQLNonNull, GraphQLField, GraphQLArgument, GraphQLDirective, every `*Kwargs`, `*Map` and `Thunk*` of them, GraphQLNamedType, GraphQLWrappingType, GraphQLType and the other type unions, graphql.resolve_thunk, strawberry.type, field, input, interface, union, enum, enum_value, scalar, directive, directive_field, schema_directive, argument, mutation, subscription, Schema, lazy, LazyType, auto, ID, Private, Parent, annotation, types, scalars, schema

capability schema/introspection  a schema asked about itself, and a schema built from what a server answered
  heroes  graphql.introspection_of, graphql.introspection_query, graphql.schema_from_introspection
  go      gqlgen introspection.Schema, Type, Field, InputValue, EnumValue, Directive, WrapSchema, WrapTypeFromDef, WrapTypeFromType, NewQuery, QueryOptions, gqlparser validator.QueryIntrospectionFields
  rust    async-graphql IntrospectionMode, juniper introspect, IntrospectionFormat, TypeKind
  python  graphql.get_introspection_query, graphql.IntrospectionQuery, graphql.introspection_from_schema, graphql.build_client_schema, graphql.introspection_types, graphql.TypeKind, graphql.SchemaMetaFieldDef, TypeMetaFieldDef, TypeNameMetaFieldDef, graphql.is_introspection_type
  note    `introspection_of` answers byte for byte what graphql-js's `introspectionFromSchema` answers on the probed schemas, the experimental deprecation of directives included as 16.15 includes it; `introspection_query` is `getIntrospectionQuery` with the settled options only

